48	 *
49	 * Rule 30 is  new = left XOR (center OR right).  The only trick is getting the
50	 * two shifts the right way round, which is genuinely easy to invert, so here is
51	 * the reasoning spelled out:
52	 *
53	 *   Bit i of `x << 1n` is bit i-1 of `x`. Bit i-1 is cell i's LEFT neighbour.
54	 *   Therefore `x << 1n` is the whole "left neighbour" plane, aligned so that
55	 *   position i holds what cell i needs.
56	 *
57	 *   Bit i of `x >> 1n` is bit i+1 of `x`, which is cell i's RIGHT neighbour.
58	 *   Therefore `x >> 1n` is the "right neighbour" plane, likewise aligned.
59	 *
